## PHASE 11 – Communication training, polish, performance and final QA

**How it works:** adds the communication practice area from the product description (self-introduction, STAR practice, filler-word drills, daily challenge) using the existing interview engine, then hardens the whole app.

**How it should behave:** communication drills reuse the same answer/evaluation services (no duplicate engines); the final QA pass removes every rough edge.

```
PHASE 11 – COMMUNICATION PRACTICE, POLISH & FINAL QA

Tasks – Communication practice (reuse existing services; no new endpoints):
1. Page /practice with cards: Self-introduction, STAR method practice (Situation/Task/Action/Result guided inputs that are combined into the answer; scorer checks all four parts), Filler-word reduction drill (short prompt, shows filler count live in voice mode or after typing), Speaking-pace drill (voice only, shows wpm vs ideal band), Daily speaking challenge (one rotating prompt per day chosen from the communication-category questions, with a streak counter stored locally).
2. Each drill creates a normal "communication" interview of 1 question through the existing flow (online or offline) so results appear in reports and progress. Show improvement tips specific to the drill.

Tasks – Polish & performance:
3. Route-level code splitting verified, bundle analysis (report size), lazy load recharts and heavy pages, image/icon optimisation, memoisation only where measured.
4. Remove duplicated components/styles/constants; ensure no hardcoded categories/roles/skills/questions outside seeds and mocks; ensure all API calls live in services.
5. Accessibility audit: keyboard-only walkthrough of the main flows, focus management in modals, labels, contrast in both themes, reduced motion. Fix findings.
6. Responsive audit at 360, 768, 1024, 1440 widths for every page. Fix overflow/alignment issues.
7. Error handling audit: simulate 401, 403, 404, 500, timeout, offline on each page and confirm friendly messages and no blank screens.
8. Console audit: zero errors and zero React warnings in a full click-through.
9. Documentation: docs/PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md (frontend part), docs/DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md (how to run with mock vs real backend, env variables, folder conventions, how to add a new category/role/language/page/setting), README frontend section, user manual (docs/USER_MANUAL.md with screenshots placeholders replaced by step lists), and a "known limitations" section (voice needs internet in most browsers, resume needs server, etc.).
10. Final test run: all unit/component tests, build, preview build (`npm run preview`) and a manual end-to-end script: guest start → offline interview → report → go online → sync; register → resume upload → generate questions → voice interview (Chrome) → report PDF → progress → settings → language switch → delete data.

Acceptance criteria:
- Lighthouse (PWA + Accessibility + Performance) results reported honestly with numbers.
- Whole app usable offline for the core interview flow.
- All tests and build pass (real output). List any open issues clearly.
```

