# PART D – SWITCHING FROM MOCK TO REAL BACKEND (do this when the backend is ready)

```
The backend is ready at <URL>. Switch from mock to real API:
1. Set VITE_USE_MOCK=false and VITE_API_URL=<URL>/api.
2. Run through every screen and compare each request/response with 00_SHARED_API_CONTRACT.md. List every mismatch (path, field name, enum, status code, response shape).
3. Fix mismatches in the frontend services only if the contract says so; if the backend deviates from the contract, report it to me instead of working around it.
4. Re-run the full manual end-to-end script and the tests, and show real results.
```

# PART E – REUSABLE "FIX" PROMPTS

**When a phase has errors:**
```
This phase has this problem: <paste exact error / console message / screenshot description>. Find the root cause, fix only what is necessary, do not change unrelated files or the API contract, re-run build and tests and show real output.
```

**For a UI change only:**
```
UI change only: <describe>. Keep the existing design system, colours and components. Change only the necessary frontend files, no API or backend changes, keep it responsive and accessible, and make sure every interaction still works.
```

**To add a new feature later:**
```
New feature: <describe>. First check whether something similar already exists. Tell me which files you will change, whether an API change is needed (if yes, stop and show the contract change first), then implement it with loading/empty/error/success states, i18n keys, offline behaviour and tests. Report what changed.
```